"A module for Drupal 10.3 and 11: a chat launcher on every page, and a "
"Smarter Chat block for any region."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: used in react/packages/smarter-llmclient-deployment/src/components/NextSteps.tsx
msgid ""
"Then, in Configuration, Web services, Smarter Chat, enter this LLMClient's "
"url."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: used in react/packages/smarter-llmclient-deployment/src/components/NextSteps.tsx
msgid ""
"A theme app extension: a chat launcher on every page, and a Smarter Chat "
"block for any section."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: used in react/packages/smarter-llmclient-deployment/src/components/NextSteps.tsx
msgid ""
"Deploy the extension as your store's own app, from a Shopify Partner "
"account, and install it on your store."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: used in react/packages/smarter-llmclient-deployment/src/components/NextSteps.tsx
msgid ""
"In the theme editor, turn on App embeds, Smarter Chat launcher, and enter "
"this LLMClient's url."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: used in react/packages/smarter-llmclient-deployment/src/components/NextSteps.tsx
msgid ""
"Allow both of your store's origins: its myshopify.com domain, and its own "
"domain."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: used in react/packages/smarter-llmclient-deployment/src/components/NextSteps.tsx
msgid "React, from npm"
msgstr ""

#. Translators: used in react/packages/smarter-llmclient-deployment/src/components/NextSteps.tsx
msgid ""
"%(package)s, the component that the workbench uses, for a React 19 "
"application built with Vite, webpack or Next.js."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: used in react/packages/smarter-llmclient-deployment/src/components/NextSteps.tsx
msgid "Any web page, in html"
msgstr ""

#. Translators: used in react/packages/smarter-llmclient-deployment/src/components/NextSteps.tsx
msgid ""
"One script tag, with no build: for a static site, a server-rendered page, "
"Squarespace, Wix or Webflow. Paste it before </body>, and a chat button "
"appears in a corner of the page."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: used in react/packages/smarter-llmclient-deployment/src/components/NextSteps.tsx
msgid ""
"The chat renders in its own Shadow DOM, so your site's css can't break it. "
"To put it inside the page instead of a launcher, add %(element)s where it "
"goes."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: used in react/packages/smarter-llmclient-deployment/src/components/NextSteps.tsx
msgid "Something else?"
msgstr ""

#. Translators: used in react/packages/smarter-llmclient-deployment/src/components/NextSteps.tsx
msgid ""
"Google Tag Manager, and documentation sites built with Docusaurus, MkDocs, "
"Sphinx or VitePress, have integrations too. Or build your own front end on "
"this url's api, below, or with the Python, Node.js and Go SDKs."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: used in react/packages/smarter-llmclient-deployment/src/components/NextSteps.tsx
msgid "Docs sites"
msgstr ""

#. Translators: used in react/packages/smarter-llmclient-deployment/src/components/NextSteps.tsx
msgid "SDKs"
msgstr ""

#. Translators: used in react/packages/smarter-llmclient-deployment/src/components/SecureUrl.tsx
msgid "Give it to Smarter Chat"
msgstr ""

#. Translators: used in react/packages/smarter-llmclient-deployment/src/components/SecureUrl.tsx
msgid ""
"Smarter Chat sends the key with every request, as %(header)s. The WordPress, "
"Drupal and Shopify integrations have an api key setting. In html, add %"
"(attribute)s:"
msgstr ""

#. Translators: used in react/packages/smarter-llmclient-deployment/src/components/SecureUrl.tsx
msgid ""
"In React, pass apiKey, from your build's environment rather than from your "
"source code:"
msgstr ""

#. Translators: used in react/packages/smarter-llmclient-deployment/src/components/SecureUrl.tsx
msgid ""
"An api key belongs to a staff user of your account, and a platform "
"administrator creates it with this command. The command prints the key's "
"name, and its secret, once: store the secret somewhere safe, such as a "
"password manager or your hosting's secrets."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: used in react/packages/smarter-llmclient-deployment/src/components/SecureUrl.tsx
msgid ""
"The web console's API Keys page lists your keys, and turns a key off without "
"deleting it."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: used in react/packages/smarter-llmclient-deployment/src/components/SecureUrl.tsx
msgid ""
"Name the key in the LLMClient's manifest, and apply the manifest again, in "
"the workbench's Manifest tab or with %(command)s. From then on, every "
"request to the url needs the key, and this page says \"Api key required\"."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: used in react/packages/smarter-llmclient-deployment/src/components/SecureUrl.tsx
msgid ""
"To replace a key, create a new one, name it in the manifest instead, and "
"apply it: Smarter detaches the old key. Then turn the old key off."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: used in react/packages/smarter-llmclient-deployment/src/components/SecureUrl.tsx
msgid "Api keys"
msgstr ""

#. Translators: used in react/packages/smarter-llmclient-deployment/src/components/SecureUrl.tsx
msgid ""
"This LLMClient already requires an api key: the url answers only requests "
"that carry one of its keys. Here is how to give a key to a front end in "
"production, and how to replace one."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: used in react/packages/smarter-llmclient-deployment/src/components/SecureUrl.tsx
msgid ""
"Right now, anyone who has this url can chat with it, and every prompt is "
"charged to its owner. Attach an api key, and the url answers only requests "
"that carry it. The workbench keeps working, with your login."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: used in react/packages/smarter-llmclient-deployment/src/components/SecureUrl.tsx
msgid "You can do it right here."
msgstr ""

#. Translators: used in react/packages/smarter-llmclient-deployment/src/components/SecureUrl.tsx
msgid "A key in a web page is not a secret"
msgstr ""

#. Translators: used in react/packages/smarter-llmclient-deployment/src/components/SecureUrl.tsx
msgid ""
"Anyone who opens the page can read the key in its source, and use it from "
"anywhere. On a public site, a key limits who can call the url, rather than "
"hiding it, so combine it with the rest:"
msgstr ""

#. Translators: used in react/packages/smarter-llmclient-deployment/src/components/SecureUrl.tsx
msgid "give each site a key of its own, and turn it off if it is abused;"
msgstr ""

